{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this module when an app’s UIKit controls should track their own activations, such as a button","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tapped or a switch flipped. The discovery runs on iOS, iPadOS, tvOS, visionOS and Mac","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Catalyst, through a ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIWindowScene","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking\/ControlActivated"},{"text":", the event it tracks, builds on every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"platform, so a tracking plan or a server can name it. SwiftUI’s controls are never tracked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automatically: give them ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackOnTap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"macOS has no equivalent; give an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSControl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"track(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing is tracked until a window scene turns it on with "},{"code":"trackControlsAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"control is named after its "},{"code":"accessibilityIdentifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", never its title or other text, which may be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a person’s data, and carries its kind, the first public UIKit class it is ("},{"code":"\"UIButton\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). By"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default a control without an identifier is skipped:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import UIKit","","final class CartViewController: UIViewController {","    let checkOut = UIButton(configuration: .filled())","","    override func viewDidLoad() {","        super.viewDidLoad()","        checkOut.accessibilityIdentifier = \"checkout-button\"  \/\/ tracked as ControlActivated(control: \"checkout-button\", kind: \"UIButton\")","        view.addSubview(checkOut)","    }","}","","\/\/ In the scene delegate's scene(_:willConnectTo:options:), beside the scene's tracker:","windowScene.traitOverrides.tracker = tracker","windowScene.trackControlsAutomatically()"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Give "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackControlsAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":" a closure to rename a control or skip it: it gets each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiscoveredControl"},{"type":"text","text":", with its identifier, kind and screen, and returns the event, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":". Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s context carries the control’s screen, the type of the view controller it is in, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenKey"},{"type":"text","text":", unless the tracker’s enrichers set one."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A touch that ends off the control tracks nothing, and neither do activations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without a touch, such as VoiceOver’s, or actions the app sends itself with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sendActions(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"except to a control the last touch was on and didn’t activate. Each activation goes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the tracker the control’s traits hold, so each scene keeps its own. The scene adds a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture recognizer to each of its windows that never recognizes, so it holds up no touch, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"swizzles nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This documentation is built on macOS, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIWindowScene"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackControlsAutomatically(_:)"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stopTrackingControlsAutomatically()"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiscoveredControl"},{"text":", have no pages here; their doc","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comments are in the sources.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also covers screen views and the app’s lifecycle."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AutomaticControlTracking"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"AutomaticControlTracking","externalID":"AutomaticControlTracking","symbolKind":"module"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"The event","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AutomaticC